# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- ObjectSpace.garbage_collect `global:` (Ruby 4.1) ---
#
# Issue #1718. Ruby 4.1's `gc.rb` adds the `global:` keyword to
# `ObjectSpace#garbage_collect` (a `module_function`, so both the singleton
# and the private instance method), as it does to `GC.start` (`gc.rbs`):
#
#   def garbage_collect full_mark: true, immediate_mark: true, immediate_sweep: true, global: true
#
# No rbs release through 4.2 declares it. Rigor does not check keyword
# names today, so this entry makes the signature correct for when it does.
# The return mirrors upstream's own `void`.
#
# TEMPORARY: delete this file once the rbs release Rigor bundles declares
# the keyword upstream.
#
# Declared unconditionally, not gated on `target_ruby` (ADR-121 § Rejected
# alternatives; false positives outrank), as `| ...` continuations of the
# upstream declarations. `global:` is optional in the added arm, which then
# answers every call the upstream arm does with the same type; a required
# keyword would switch `call.wrong-arity` off for the method (see `gc.rbs`).
module ObjectSpace
  def self.garbage_collect: (?full_mark: bool, ?immediate_mark: bool, ?immediate_sweep: bool, ?global: boolish) -> void
                          | ...

  def garbage_collect: (?full_mark: bool, ?immediate_mark: bool, ?immediate_sweep: bool, ?global: boolish) -> void
                     | ...
end
